1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:22,210
Let Hsieh Tien-ti go.

3
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,330
I went against the will of Kakarayan

4
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:26,090
and let her live.

5
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:28,460
I'm the one who should
take responsibility, not her.

6
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,350
Responsibility?

7
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:33,080
How will you take responsibility?

8
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:35,630
When I find a way to reconnect
with Kakarayan,

9
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:37,970
I'll explain everything to Him myself.

10
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:40,520
Do whatever you want with me then.

11
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:42,150
No.

12
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,770
I can't postpone
dealing with Hsieh Tien-ti

13
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,800
until you've gotten in touch with Him.

14
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:47,380
My job

15
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:49,890
is to ensure the order of cause and effect

16
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:52,620
follows what Kakarayan has planned.

17
00:00:52,710 --> 00:00:54,470
No one can change that.

18
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:56,530
You're no exception.

19
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,510
Erase Hsieh Tien-ti's memory

20
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,860
and take her back to the beginning.

21
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:04,230
This is your last chance.

22
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:07,140
It's your last chance
to make things right,

23
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:09,250
considering you were the messenger.

24
00:01:11,539 --> 00:01:13,380
Then...

25
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:16,990
we can go back to Pinokayan together

26
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:20,030
and wrap up

27
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,180
the earthly task

28
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:25,920
that was given to us by Kakarayan.

29
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:39,920
Don't believe Fali.

30
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,250
Just like you never believed me.

31
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:56,590
[Mountain Travel]

32
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:59,320
Is it okay for me to use this photo?

33
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:01,030
It's pretty.

34
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,010
Won't it be weird to put it like that?

35
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,250
No.

36
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:05,790
That was close.

37
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:09,259
Then...

38
00:02:09,389 --> 00:02:11,070
what about this?

39
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:12,960
I took this one, didn't I?

40
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:14,940
I don't think so.

41
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:15,950
I did.

42
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,720
Did you take it?

43
00:02:21,270 --> 00:02:22,110
Hey.

44
00:02:24,050 --> 00:02:25,060
Don't bother.

45
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,650
Sung-en's trip has been canceled.

46
00:02:28,670 --> 00:02:29,550
Why?

47
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:31,440
Because...

48
00:02:32,450 --> 00:02:34,829
she's not in her best condition lately.

49
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,860
So we decided to let her rest.

50
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:42,220
I worked on it for so long though.

51
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:45,300
It's okay. Never mind.

52
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,020
Sung-en is sick to begin with.

53
00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:49,829
When she gets better,

54
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,850
let's plan a new itinerary for her.

55
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:55,280
Yes.

56
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,010
Well...

57
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,420
You should go home now.

58
00:02:59,510 --> 00:03:00,210
Thank you for the hard work.

59
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,710
-Okay, bye.
-I'm leaving.

60
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,850
Bye.

61
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,650
I need a pick-me-up.

62
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:17,150
Is there a good café these days?

63
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,900
This place is very famous.
I want to try it.

64
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,310
Where is it?

65
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:27,450
But you need to line up
for hours to get in.

66
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:28,810
I'll line up for you.

67
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:31,630
Are you sure?

68
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:34,490
But on one condition.

69
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:37,300
If I get in line,

70
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:40,780
think of it as our date.

71
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,100
Okay.

72
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,920
Do you mean it?

73
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:52,310
I'll leave it to you then.

74
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:53,980
See you later.

75
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:03,530
Right, I forgot to tell you.

76
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:05,240
Ting-yi is coming too.

77
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,910
Ting-yi?

78
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,750
Also,

79
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,950
please clear the table for me. Bye.

80
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,320
Hello, everyone.

81
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:39,740
I'm Shi Shi, Sun Sheng Xi.

82
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:42,510
I'll sing a new song for you today.

83
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,740
I hope you like it.

84
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:59,270
♫ The crowd is big, I'm fading fast ♫

85
00:04:59,450 --> 00:05:04,640
♫ With just one look, you can save ♫

86
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:12,250
♫ Loneliness made me wander endlessly ♫

87
00:05:12,650 --> 00:05:17,310
♫ You reach out to me
as I stand on the edge ♫

88
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:21,400
♫ The prideful humans,
you're all-powerful ♫

89
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:24,750
♫ But you've lost to time ♫

90
00:05:25,010 --> 00:05:30,330
♫ Where else can we go? ♫

91
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:33,990
[Mountain Travel]

92
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:33,940
"The criteria of my ideal man.
Height, 188."

93
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:35,090
Impossible.

94
00:05:35,170 --> 00:05:36,050
"Lean."

95
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:36,980
Impossible.

96
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:38,030
"Long fingers."

97
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:39,180
Impossible.

98
00:05:39,930 --> 00:05:40,890
Long fingers?

99
00:05:42,570 --> 00:05:44,940
I think I have pretty long fingers.

100
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,810
'Orad, what are you doing here?

101
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:50,090
Where's Hsieh Tien-ti?

102
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:51,760
Tien-ti left a long time ago.

103
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:53,210
She left?

104
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:55,409
Did she say where she was going?

105
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,659
She didn't say where.

106
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:00,250
What's the matter?

107
00:06:01,350 --> 00:06:02,100
Thank you.

108
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:03,910
Bye, 'Orad.

109
00:06:13,150 --> 00:06:15,790
[The number you have dialed
is unavailable.]

110
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,840
That's weird. Where did she go?

111
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:39,940
[Maybe right from the start,]

112
00:06:40,030 --> 00:06:41,390
I shouldn't have tried to change

113
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,240
the Reflection of Time you saw

114
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:45,570
about my death.

115
00:06:45,659 --> 00:06:46,850
Maybe I should've done

116
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,140
what Fali had told me to.

117
00:06:50,150 --> 00:06:52,080
This life belongs to her.

118
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,600
I should give it back to her.

119
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:00,930
[Feeling regret]

120
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:04,320
[won't undo what has happened.]

121
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,420
I'm a human.

122
00:07:06,870 --> 00:07:08,940
I'm not a Kawas.

123
00:07:09,070 --> 00:07:10,960
Kawas like you,

124
00:07:11,050 --> 00:07:11,880
who always just stood by

125
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:13,470
and watched what happened

126
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,830
will never know

127
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,370
[how painful it is for us]

128
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:18,260
[who are living through it.]

129
00:07:28,290 --> 00:07:30,930
[So for the world,]

130
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:33,130
[the one who should live]

131
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:35,420
[is her and not me.]

132
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:48,710
♫ The crowd is big, I'm fading fast ♫

133
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:54,030
♫ With just one look, you can save ♫

134
00:07:54,870 --> 00:08:01,690
♫ Loneliness made me wander endlessly ♫

135
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:06,790
♫ You reach out to me
as I stand on the edge ♫

136
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:10,710
♫ The prideful humans,
you're all-powerful ♫

137
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:14,400
♫ But you've lost to time ♫

138
00:08:14,490 --> 00:08:19,860
♫ Where else can we go? ♫

139
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:25,930
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

140
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:32,220
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

141
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:34,470
[This is what I thought.]

142
00:08:33,590 --> 00:08:40,100
♫ The rain will never end,
but I won't hold an umbrella ♫

143
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:37,809
[Humans are weaker than I thought.]

144
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:44,940
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

145
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:49,520
♫ I'm not a god,
I don't have to be generous ♫

146
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:52,600
♫ Please let me love you selfishly ♫

147
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:54,360
♫ When the souls come together,

148
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:57,610
♫ I'm no longer afraid of regret ♫

149
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,770
[So this is your new plan.]

150
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:02,360
♫ If I went back to the beginning,
what would I choose? ♫

151
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:01,570
[To let Hsieh Tien-ti die again]

152
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,550
[because of your lies?]

153
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:05,440
♫ Light a light for me ♫

154
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:04,920
[And in order to save her,]

155
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,110
['Orad, once again unknowingly,]

156
00:09:05,530 --> 00:09:07,380
♫ So that the souls can reunite ♫

157
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:08,650
[from being the messenger of Kakarayan,]

158
00:09:07,470 --> 00:09:10,810
♫ And be convinced when they're leaving ♫

159
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:11,030
he'll become your own messenger.

160
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:13,230
There's nothing new about that.

161
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:21,900
♫ Since we crossed paths,
it had to have existed ♫

162
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:17,890
You're wrong.

163
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:21,020
My goal from the beginning

164
00:09:21,150 --> 00:09:24,450
was not just 'Orad.

165
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:27,440
♫ With each memory, you protected me ♫

166
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:26,560
It pertains to all the Kawas,

167
00:09:26,690 --> 00:09:28,850
including Kakarayan.

168
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:34,350
♫ There is no forever,
so it should burn even more ♫

169
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:33,290
Over the years,

170
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,640
I thought the humans were the ones

171
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:39,450
♫ If you understand me a little,
then I'll be happy ♫

172
00:09:36,730 --> 00:09:39,010
making the world worse.

173
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:43,630
♫ The prideful humans,
you're all-powerful ♫

174
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:42,930
But I realized I was wrong.

175
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:47,110
♫ But you've lost to time ♫

176
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:46,450
The one who ruined this world

177
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:47,950
is not the humans.

178
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:52,570
♫ Where else can we go? ♫

179
00:09:49,350 --> 00:09:50,890
It's God.

180
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:54,240
It's those spirits who can't help

181
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:56,440
♫ You connected
the dotted line toward me ♫

182
00:09:54,330 --> 00:09:57,760
but have a soft spot for humans.

183
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:59,960
♫ I call that yearning ♫

184
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:05,940
♫ Turns out
I was wide awake in this dream ♫

185
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,860
Does that door

186
00:10:02,950 --> 00:10:04,930
really lead to Pinokayan?

187
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:11,530
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

188
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:18,740
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

189
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,620
You finally understand

190
00:10:16,370 --> 00:10:18,700
why I've kept you alive until now, right?

191
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:25,780
♫ The rain will never end,
but I won't hold an umbrella ♫

192
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,160
Toem, the goddess of clouds

193
00:10:21,250 --> 00:10:23,410
that exposes deceit and controls lies.

194
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:24,990
Do you know

195
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:30,710
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

196
00:10:26,310 --> 00:10:27,720
why I choose to tell you this

197
00:10:27,810 --> 00:10:29,390
at this moment?

198
00:10:31,770 --> 00:10:32,870
Because...

199
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:38,280
♫ Rain falls as the crowd disperses ♫

200
00:10:34,890 --> 00:10:36,780
in this world,

201
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:39,820
you're the only person
'Orad doesn't trust.

202
00:10:38,370 --> 00:10:44,400
♫ Let the limited become unlimited,
you can't leave just yet ♫

203
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,440
Even if it's the truth,

204
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:51,040
♫ Please stop wandering,
please control me ♫

205
00:10:45,630 --> 00:10:47,520
it becomes a lie, like a fleeting cloud,

206
00:10:48,490 --> 00:10:51,130
when it comes from you.

207
00:10:51,130 --> 00:10:57,150
♫ Suddenly, it's too bright ♫

208
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,780
The more you want to tell him the truth,

209
00:10:54,910 --> 00:10:56,270
the more he'll believe

210
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,650
everything I've told him.

211
00:10:57,240 --> 00:11:02,350
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

212
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:09,170
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

213
00:11:05,870 --> 00:11:07,320
And they're lies.

214
00:11:10,350 --> 00:11:17,170
♫ The rain will never end,
but I won't hold an umbrella ♫

215
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:21,790
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

216
00:11:22,810 --> 00:11:28,390
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

217
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:35,610
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

218
00:11:36,010 --> 00:11:42,740
♫ The rain will never end,
but I won't hold an umbrella ♫

219
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:47,620
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

220
00:11:53,690 --> 00:11:55,140
What's your problem?

221
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,120
Get up. You hit someone.

222
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,460
You're heavy. Get up.

223
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:01,740
Hurry up. I want to go for another round.

224
00:12:04,250 --> 00:12:06,320
I know you won't believe anything I say.

225
00:12:06,410 --> 00:12:08,390
But I really can't let you
go see her right now.

226
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,290
Move aside.

227
00:12:28,190 --> 00:12:29,640
You can't just leave
after hitting someone.

228
00:12:41,430 --> 00:12:42,660
Move aside!

229
00:14:38,290 --> 00:14:41,330
♫ Happy birthday to you ♫

230
00:14:41,410 --> 00:14:42,910
Thank you.

231
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:43,610
Make a wish.

232
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:45,550
I want ten wishes.

233
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,960
That's too many.

234
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:48,720
-It's okay. I made a hundred last time.
-I knew it.

235
00:14:48,810 --> 00:14:50,300
A hundred wishes are okay

236
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:52,150
Having me is your biggest wish.

237
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,000
[When is your birthday?]

238
00:14:54,830 --> 00:14:56,730
You have a lot of questions today.

239
00:14:56,810 --> 00:14:59,320
First, you asked about my name.
Now, you ask about my birthday.

240
00:14:59,810 --> 00:15:00,770
You're my guardian angel.

241
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,840
Is it wrong for me to want
to know more about you?

242
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,830
Hurry up. The date.

243
00:15:05,970 --> 00:15:06,930
I don't have a birthday.

244
00:15:07,770 --> 00:15:11,250
You're lying.
How can you not have a birthday?

245
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,010
It's true.

246
00:15:14,110 --> 00:15:15,510
Even if I did, I had forgotten it.

247
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,150
It has been thousands of years.

248
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:22,550
So you've never celebrated your birthday?

249
00:15:24,970 --> 00:15:27,740
Then how will you make a birthday wish?

250
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:31,920
I'm the messenger of Kakarayan.

251
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:34,480
I don't need wishes.

252
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,820
Why doesn't the messenger

253
00:15:37,910 --> 00:15:39,230
need to make wishes?

254
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,250
The future has already been decided.

255
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,410
So why make a wish?

256
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:47,280
Even so, you can still make a wish.

257
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:53,260
I don't celebrate my birthday
nor do I make wishes.

258
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:54,360
Are you satisfied?

259
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:55,950
[Stop asking me questions.]

260
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,410
[I don't believe you.]

261
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,480
[How is it possible
that you've never made a wish?]

262
00:16:00,610 --> 00:16:02,990
[Haven't you ever had a moment]

263
00:16:03,650 --> 00:16:06,240
where you knew you couldn't do it,

264
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:08,620
but you had to get something done

265
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:11,220
no matter what?

266
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,800
[No.]

267
00:16:12,890 --> 00:16:14,340
[Are you serious?]

268
00:16:14,430 --> 00:16:15,480
[Yes, never.]

269
00:16:15,570 --> 00:16:17,680
[Never?]

270
00:16:17,770 --> 00:16:19,180
[There was never a moment]

271
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:24,370
[when you felt utterly hopeless
and could only plead with God?]

272
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:35,590
[I'm the messenger of Kakarayan.]

273
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:38,760
[I don't need wishes.]

274
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:54,250
I'm begging you.

275
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,750
As long as she lives,

276
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:01,330
I will pay any price for it.

277
00:17:17,210 --> 00:17:20,640
[God's righteousness is not to make
you submit. Submission stems from fear]

278
00:17:21,130 --> 00:17:24,560
[God's righteousness is for you
to surrender yourself completely]

279
00:17:24,650 --> 00:17:30,100
[When you hand yourself to God,
He will deliver you]

280
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:31,200
I'm sorry.

281
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:36,090
[Let God lead you. Tell God what you need]

282
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,520
This is the last time I'm lying to you.

283
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,560
If...

284
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,690
you can hear my voice,

285
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,370
please let me see her

286
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,770
as soon as I open my eyes.

287
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:31,350
[Let God lead you. Tell God what you need]

288
00:18:36,410 --> 00:18:41,210
[What you believe is the deity's will
and what God sees is the truth]

289
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:01,500
How did you...

290
00:20:01,590 --> 00:20:02,820
What are you doing here?

291
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,850
Do you know I've been looking for you?

292
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,050
I just...

293
00:20:07,130 --> 00:20:08,450
What are you doing?

294
00:20:08,590 --> 00:20:10,170
Nothing.

295
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,240
I was just thinking.

296
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:15,360
If I could change

297
00:20:15,490 --> 00:20:18,130
the Reflection of Time you saw,

298
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,380
does that mean it's possible

299
00:20:21,170 --> 00:20:23,020
to let Sung-en live?

300
00:20:24,910 --> 00:20:26,360
Why are you here?

301
00:20:26,930 --> 00:20:28,650
And the ring...

302
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:31,470
Did you regain your powers
as the messenger?

303
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:37,360
♫ The crowd is big ♫

304
00:20:38,150 --> 00:20:41,320
♫ I'm fading fast ♫

305
00:20:41,450 --> 00:20:42,550
♫ With just one look ♫

306
00:20:42,690 --> 00:20:44,310
This scene...

307
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:46,030
I saw it in the Reflection of Time.

308
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:48,190
♫ Loneliness made me ♫

309
00:20:48,270 --> 00:20:49,590
Tien-ti!

310
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:52,890
♫ Wander endlessly ♫

311
00:20:53,030 --> 00:20:54,520
This is what I told you before.

312
00:20:54,610 --> 00:20:56,060
I heard a woman singing.

313
00:20:56,150 --> 00:20:57,420
This is the Reflection of Time

314
00:20:57,510 --> 00:20:59,670
where a lot of people collapsed.

315
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:00,240
Reflection of Time?

316
00:21:00,370 --> 00:21:03,280
♫ The prideful humans,
you're all-powerful ♫

317
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:06,880
♫ But you've lost to time ♫

318
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:12,910
♫ Where else can we go? ♫

319
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:18,680
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

320
00:21:19,690 --> 00:21:25,140
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

321
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:29,280
♫ The rain will never end ♫

322
00:21:29,370 --> 00:21:33,280
♫ But I won't hold an umbrella ♫

323
00:21:33,370 --> 00:21:37,820
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

324
00:22:06,110 --> 00:22:08,390
This is your house.

325
00:22:12,270 --> 00:22:13,760
Are we really back?

326
00:22:13,850 --> 00:22:15,080
How could this happen?

327
00:22:15,210 --> 00:22:16,970
So not only can you teleport,

328
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:18,600
but your house is back too.

329
00:22:18,690 --> 00:22:19,390
Does that mean

330
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:21,810
you've recovered all your powers?

331
00:22:21,950 --> 00:22:23,180
I...

332
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:25,640
What did you do? How did you do it?

333
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:29,290
I'm not sure.

334
00:22:30,260 --> 00:22:31,930
But while looking for you,

335
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:33,560
I ran into some trouble.

336
00:22:34,750 --> 00:22:35,590
Then...

337
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:38,930
when I thought I'd never see you again,

338
00:22:40,290 --> 00:22:42,760
I tried to do something.

339
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:44,340
What is it?

340
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:47,640
I made a wish to Kakarayan.

341
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:49,970
You made a wish?

342
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:51,780
Yes.

343
00:22:53,050 --> 00:22:56,840
When I opened my eyes
after making the wish,

344
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:59,040
I was right at the intersection.

345
00:23:02,250 --> 00:23:03,300
We need to hurry back.

346
00:23:03,390 --> 00:23:04,490
Hurry back?

347
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:05,680
That woman...

348
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:08,190
We have to stop her.

349
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:09,200
That woman

350
00:23:09,330 --> 00:23:10,560
and the white footprints she left behind.

351
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:11,840
I saw them

352
00:23:11,970 --> 00:23:13,420
in the Reflection of Time.

353
00:23:13,510 --> 00:23:16,020
She's the reason all those people
became unconscious.

354
00:23:16,110 --> 00:23:17,740
Wait for me here.

355
00:23:17,910 --> 00:23:19,100
I'll be right back.

356
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,460
[Yi-han]

357
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:23,760
[Have you secured a spot at the cafe?]

358
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:24,640
[Pu]

359
00:23:23,850 --> 00:23:24,600
[Don't rush me.]

360
00:23:24,690 --> 00:23:25,920
[Hurry up.]

361
00:23:24,730 --> 00:23:25,700
[Yi-han]

362
00:23:25,790 --> 00:23:28,560
[Pu]

363
00:23:26,010 --> 00:23:28,470
[Yes, I'm on my way. Just a second.]

364
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:39,910
Sir.

365
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,190
Are you okay?

366
00:23:41,270 --> 00:23:44,490
Hey.

367
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:53,860
Right now,

368
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:54,780
we are at the place

369
00:23:54,910 --> 00:23:57,110
where a crowd suddenly fell unconscious.

370
00:23:57,250 --> 00:23:58,210
The police estimates

371
00:23:58,350 --> 00:23:59,970
that there are currently 247 people

372
00:24:00,060 --> 00:24:02,130
who were sent to the hospital nearby.

373
00:24:02,220 --> 00:24:03,580
But due to more unconscious people

374
00:24:03,670 --> 00:24:05,120
being discovered,

375
00:24:05,210 --> 00:24:06,130
the actual casualty number

376
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:08,250
-will undoubtedly rise.
-Someone is unconscious here!

377
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:52,110
If you want to be happy, go get it.

378
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:54,620
Get it from them.

379
00:24:52,290 --> 00:25:21,810
[Next episode]

380
00:24:54,710 --> 00:24:55,980
[That's how people of this world]

381
00:24:56,070 --> 00:24:57,130
[do it anyway.]

382
00:24:57,220 --> 00:24:58,360
[Could it be]

383
00:24:58,450 --> 00:24:59,680
that the place the Kawas went to

384
00:24:59,770 --> 00:25:01,400
was not Pinokayan after all?

385
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:03,550
Because you could have changed it.

386
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,090
But I couldn't persuade you.

387
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:06,940
Who are you to save him?

388
00:25:07,030 --> 00:25:08,130
Are you saving him as a friend

389
00:25:08,220 --> 00:25:10,240
or as the messenger of Kakarayan?

390
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:12,130
Or do you already

391
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:14,160
think of yourself as Kakarayan?

392
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,480
You should know

393
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,590
how I can meet Kakarayan, right?

394
00:25:17,810 --> 00:25:20,800
[Go through the door and you'll meet Him.]

395
00:25:28,670 --> 00:25:29,690
Tien-ti.

396
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:41,830
[1998, What is this called?]

397
00:25:30,170 --> 00:25:32,370
Hurry up and pack your things.

398
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:35,010
Your parents will pick you up later.

399
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:36,990
Okay, hold on.

400
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,010
Halikien.

401
00:25:41,210 --> 00:25:42,050
If you won't listen,

402
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:44,250
I'm going to wash your dog.

403
00:25:44,340 --> 00:25:45,530
No, don't!

404
00:25:45,660 --> 00:25:47,420
Halikien!

405
00:25:52,430 --> 00:25:55,690
Grandma, what are you talking about?
I don't understand.

406
00:25:56,790 --> 00:25:58,640
I said, "Halikien."

407
00:25:58,730 --> 00:26:01,500
It means "hurry up."

408
00:26:01,590 --> 00:26:03,520
Is that what you tell the Kawas

409
00:26:03,610 --> 00:26:05,770
when you're trying to heal the sick?

410
00:26:05,850 --> 00:26:08,890
Yes, I say that to the Kawas.

411
00:26:09,810 --> 00:26:13,470
How do you say "road"
in the Kawas language?

412
00:26:14,350 --> 00:26:16,060
Road is called...

413
00:26:17,950 --> 00:26:18,700
"lalan."

414
00:26:20,860 --> 00:26:22,530
What about flowers?

415
00:26:22,620 --> 00:26:24,290
Flowers are called...

416
00:26:24,380 --> 00:26:25,920
"falo."

417
00:26:28,250 --> 00:26:31,420
Then what is that called?

418
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:35,730
The sky is called "Kakarayan."

419
00:26:35,820 --> 00:26:36,700
No.

420
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:40,220
I'm asking about the rain
that falls from the sky.

421
00:26:40,610 --> 00:26:42,590
The rain that falls from the sky?

422
00:26:42,810 --> 00:26:44,220
It's called...

423
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:47,650
"'Orad."

424
00:26:48,930 --> 00:26:51,130
See? It's raining.

425
00:26:53,860 --> 00:26:56,230
It's really raining. Hurry!

426
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:01,560
It's a downpour.

427
00:27:01,640 --> 00:27:03,620
Come here, let me dry you up.

428
00:27:03,710 --> 00:27:05,690
You're all wet.

429
00:27:05,780 --> 00:27:07,100
Grandma.

430
00:27:07,230 --> 00:27:09,040
Let me tell you a secret.

431
00:27:09,170 --> 00:27:10,580
What secret?

432
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:14,270
I like 'Orad.

433
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:17,530
You like 'Orad?

434
00:27:18,410 --> 00:27:19,900
Do you really like 'Orad?

435
00:27:20,830 --> 00:27:24,520
Okay, I'll take you and the dog
to find 'Orad.

436
00:27:24,650 --> 00:27:25,050
All right?

437
00:27:25,140 --> 00:27:25,800
Okay.

438
00:27:25,890 --> 00:27:26,990
Really?

439
00:27:28,790 --> 00:27:30,200
-Are you ready?
-Yes.

440
00:27:29,100 --> 00:27:34,600
♫ I can't see you, but I know ♫

441
00:27:30,290 --> 00:27:31,610
One.

442
00:27:31,690 --> 00:27:32,930
Two.

443
00:27:33,060 --> 00:27:34,030
Three.

444
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,610
Go!

445
00:27:35,700 --> 00:27:41,860
♫ The sky is clear after the rain,
reminding me to be well ♫

446
00:27:43,490 --> 00:27:48,590
♫ I can't hear you, but I know ♫

447
00:27:49,690 --> 00:27:55,810
♫ The shadow that hangs on the melody
are symbols of yearning ♫

448
00:27:56,820 --> 00:27:58,580
♫ Come on ♫

449
00:27:58,670 --> 00:28:02,710
♫ Let's go back to the beginning ♫

450
00:28:03,860 --> 00:28:10,150
♫ Just like when you were by my side ♫

451
00:28:10,900 --> 00:28:17,190
♫ I'll always be here waiting for you,
calling you ♫

452
00:28:17,940 --> 00:28:25,060
♫ Show me the way to find you ♫
